,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":-0.017823083552581886,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":16.1,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.06282005442244139,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":80.9,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.0013886834547587323,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":51.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.013645917111384631,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":77.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.32125,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Global Indemnity Group, LLC, through its subsidiaries, provides specialty property and casualty insurance, and reinsurance products in the United States. It operates through three segments: Agency and Insurance Services; Belmont Core; and Belmont Non-Core. The company engages in sourcing, underwriting, and servicing primary and assumed reinsurance business; and providing technology, AI-enabled marketplace, and claims services. It also distributes property and general liability products for small commercial businesses and for owners of properties under construction, under renovation, vacant, or rented through a select network of wholesale general agents with specific binding authority. In addition, the company offers property and general liability niche products; property coverage for owners of collectible items; and individual treaties with small-to-medium sized financially sound insurers in niche product lines, contracted through reinsurance brokers/intermediaries. Global Indemnity Group, LLC was founded in 2003 and is headquartered in Bala Cynwyd, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Praveen K. Reddy | President & CEO of Penn-America Underwriters, LLC","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 286 people. Revenue per employee of $1.6M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers. Stock-based compensation of $21K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Global Indemnity Group, LLC is a small-cap financial services business with a $318M market cap on $450M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -11% over the past three years and -2% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 32% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 22% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 24% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Valued at a 48% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Global Indemnity Group Llc Class A (de) (GBLI) Affects Rotational Strategy Timing","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/132/How_Global_Indemnity_Group_Llc_Class_A_de_GBLI_Affects_Rotational_Strategy_Timing_110526070801_1793880481.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793880481.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Global Indemnity Group (NASDAQ:GBLI) Releases Quarterly Earnings Results","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/global-indemnity-group-nasdaqgbli-releases-quarterly-earnings-results.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793815850.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.273,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Global Indemnity GAAP EPS of $0.61 (NASDAQ:GBLI)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4